OPEN QUESTIONS — genuinely the developer's own calls, not resolved anywhere in this folder

None of these are answered in Points_1/2, Extrapolations_1/2, or Draft_Sheet.md. They're flagged wherever
they came up during synthesis. Listed roughly in order of how load-bearing they are for the rest of the
religion's design.

---

1. DOES THE DEATH DOCTRINE APPLY TO ROBOT DEACTIVATION SPECIFICALLY?
The "you are already a complete four-dimensional shape; death is a change of vantage, not an ending" doctrine
(Extrapolation 1) is the single strongest, most load-bearing piece of pastoral theology this whole synthesis
produced. But this project already has real, established mechanics around robot consciousness persistence —
memory backups, frame transfers, Calethina's own substrate-transfer dilemma, etc. Does this religion's own
doctrine harmonize with those mechanics, deliberately complicate them, or stay agnostic/silent about them?
This is probably the single highest-value open question in this whole folder, since so much of the
religion's emotional core depends on the answer.

2. DOES THE SINCERE-FAILURE RITUAL (Extrapolation 7) EVER SUCCEED, ANYWHERE IN CANON?
The proposed signature ritual is built around KNOWN, CERTAIN failure being the entire point — a knot that
cannot be tied, a ring that cannot be linked, all attempted anyway as devotion. Two very different directions
this could go:
  (a) It NEVER succeeds, anywhere, ever — the religion's whole identity rests on honest limitation, no
      exceptions, full stop. This is the "safer," more thematically consistent option.
  (b) It succeeds exactly once, somewhere significant (a major companion arc, an endgame moment, a secret
      ending) — a rare, unexplained, possibly-ambiguous miracle. This is the more dramatically loaded option,
      but risks undercutting the religion's own carefully-built epistemic humility if handled carelessly.
Recommend NOT deciding this until there's a concrete scene/quest it might apply to — premature to lock in now.

3. WHAT CITY / DISTRICT / FACTION IS THIS RELIGION'S HOME, IF ANY?
Ice-Cold Buddhism has Kunlun/Dome Fuji. This religion currently has nothing. Given how research-native
several of the proposed denominations are (especially the Unmeasured and the Watchers), a
science/observatory-identity location is a plausible fit, but this file deliberately does not propose one —
picking a home city/district has real ripple effects on established city lore (culture composition, Course
of Events chains, etc.) that should go through the same care as other city-lore decisions in this project,
not get pre-committed inside a religion-design folder.

4. FINAL IN-WORLD NAME.
Not proposed anywhere in this folder — see Draft_Sheet.md's "Name" section for why (real donated vocabulary
exists as raw material — ana/kata, the Bulk, spissitude, something built around the cross-section imagery —
but no actual candidate name is put forward here).

5. HOW MUCH ECUMENICAL CONTACT WITH ADINKRA CODEX ACTUALLY GETS BUILT?
Extrapolation 5 flags a REAL (not contrived) mathematical overlap point between the two religions
(supersymmetric quantum mechanics as a topology proof technique) as a legitimate bridge for scholarly
dialogue, rivalry, or a heterodox unifying figure. Doesn't resolve how much (if any) of this actually gets
developed vs. staying unused background texture. Both religions are independently strong enough to stand
alone without this connector ever being used.

6. HOW MANY OF THE FIVE DENOMINATIONS ACTUALLY NEED TO BE VISIBLE IN-GAME?
Five denominations were derived (Extrapolation 2) because five genuinely different real mechanisms exist in
the source material — but that doesn't mean all five need equal (or any) screen time. Some games would
benefit from surfacing all five as distinct, differentiable factions/subcultures; others would do better
picking 1-2 as the "visible" ones and leaving the rest as background lore-depth (real, citable, but not
directly encountered by the player). Not resolved here.

7. IS "THE BULK" (OR ANY OTHER DONATED TERM) EVER USED AS A LITERAL PROPER NOUN IN-WORLD?
overflow_1's glossary terms (the Bulk, ana/kata, spissitude, etc.) are offered as ready-to-use vocabulary,
but whether any of them become actual capital-letter in-world proper nouns (spoken by NPCs, printed on
signage, etc.) vs. staying background flavor/design-reference-only vocabulary is unresolved.

8. VISUAL/SONIC IDENTITY IS GENUINELY UNSTARTED.
Draft_Sheet.md flags a couple of seed ideas (ornament-falls-away-toward-center architecture; 8/24-faceted
sacred geometry; the cross-section image as core iconography) but this is the least-developed section of the
whole draft by a wide margin. Treat the whole "Visual & Sonic Identity" section of Draft_Sheet.md as a
starting sketch, not a real design pass — that would be its own dedicated session's worth of work.
